-- title:
--   Level automorphisms moving the Igusa Gauss ring displace centres
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $5 \le q$ and $M'$ a nonzero level with $q \nmid M'$; $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. The finset $W$ of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ is required by `hW` to consist exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, that is of the places $w$ that are rational, are affine geometric places, and satisfy $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(j_{\mathrm{geom}}) \in \mathrm{ssJSet}\,q$. The hypothesis `hle` states $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, the latter being the geometric function field $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\cdot F(\Gamma_H(q^2M'))$ for $H = \mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$, realised inside Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Further, $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ (a valuation subring with surjective residue map whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ and its residue map, together with the order- and degree-compatibility clauses of that structure), and `hR₀` pins $R_0$ down as coefficientwise reduction: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image in Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Finally $\zeta$ is a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (an element of `Idx q`), and two families of valuation subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ are given: $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ indexed by the projective line $\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{Z}/q)$ and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ indexed by $W$.
--
--   The Igusa group of hypotheses consists of: `hIg_inf`, which says that $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ is the Gauss ring, $f$ lying in it exactly when there are Laurent series $x,y$ with coefficients in $A$ such that the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ is nonzero and $f \cdot x(y) = x(x)$ after pushing $x,y$ into Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; `hIg`, which says that every $\ell \in \mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{Z}/q)$ is of the form $\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma \cdot \mathrm{lineInfty}\,q$ for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the pullback of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$; `hIg_inj`, injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$; and `hIg_perm`, which says that for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ the pullback along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ permutes the family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$, i.e. equals $O_{\mathrm{Ig}} \circ \sigma$ for some permutation $\sigma$ of $\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{Z}/q)$.
--
--   The supersingular group consists of: `hSS_A`, that for each $s \in W$ an element of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ precisely when it lies in $A$; `hSS_over`, that for $s \in W$ and $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ which has non-negative order at every place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ at which $j_q$ has non-negative order, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, and for every $a \in A$ with $\mathrm{residue}_A(a) = s.\mathrm{evalAt}(R_0.\mathrm{residue}\,f)$ the difference of that image and $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$; `hSS_fix`, that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is invariant under pullback along every $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; and `hSS_tr`, that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ contains an element $t$ with $t - a$ a unit of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ for every $a \in A$. In addition, $R$ is a `RegularProlongation` of $A$ from $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ to $\mathrm{xHFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,(q^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$ with $R.\mathrm{integers} = O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ (`hR`), and `hR₀O` identifies $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ with the preimage of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ under the inclusion of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$.
--
--   The arithmetic group of hypotheses on the base fixes: an element $\pi \in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$; an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$ such that the contraction $A \cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is henselian, and has algebraically closed residue field, together with `hκ`, that every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some element of $k_0$ lying in $A$; an auxiliary prime $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \neq q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$, an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$; and a finite extension $K_1$ of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with a valuation subring $A_1$ of $K_1$ which is the contraction of $A$ (`hA₁`), $A_1$ being a henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   The conclusion is stated for $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. It asserts: for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $k_0$ such that (i) the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ together with $F_0$ is everything, (ii) $F_0$ is stable under every $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, (iii) for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and every $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ with all $a_i$ in the compositum $T(K') := k_0(\text{image of }K') \sqcup F_0$, linear independence of $c$ over $K'$ and $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ force all $a_i = 0$, and (iv) $F_0$ contains every element of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ whose Laurent series has rational coefficients: then, for every $A_1$-algebra structure on $T_1 := T(K_1)$ whose structure map agrees with the inclusion $K_1 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ on $A_1$, and for every $j_1 \in T_1$ whose image in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ is the $q$-expansion $j_q$ with coefficients in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, with $j_1 \neq 0$, the following holds for the two-chart integral model $\mathfrak{X} := \mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel}\,A_1\,T_1\,j_1$ over $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$, the pushout of the two charts $X_{\mathrm{Fin}} = \operatorname{Spec}$ of the integral closure of $A_1[j_1]$ in $T_1$ and $X_{\mathrm{Inf}} = \operatorname{Spec}$ of the integral closure of $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$.
--
--   Four auxiliary predicates are introduced. For $x \in \mathfrak{X}$ and $f \in T_1$, $\mathrm{InStalk}\,x\,f$ says that for every point $y$ of $X_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ mapping to $x$ under $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ there are $g,h$ in the finite chart algebra with $h \notin y$ and $f h = g$, and likewise on the infinite chart; $\mathrm{InMax}\,x\,f$ adds to each clause the requirement $g \in y$. For a place $P$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, $\mathrm{Centred}\,P\,x$ says that $P$ is rational (the structure map to its residue field is surjective) and that every $f$ with $\mathrm{InStalk}\,x\,f$ lies in $P.\mathrm{toValuationSubring}$, has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and satisfies $A.\mathrm{valuation}(P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f) < 1$ if and only if $\mathrm{InMax}\,x\,f$. $\mathrm{GoodPt}\,x$ is the conjunction of: $x$ maps to the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$; $x$ is closed (every $y$ to which $x$ specialises equals $x$); every element $b$ of either chart algebra, at a point $y$ of that chart over $x$, whose image in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ is a non-unit of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ lies in $y$; and for every point $y$ of the finite chart over $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the finite chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j_1)$ is not in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q\,\Omega$ (the set of $j$ with all $q$-torsion of every elliptic curve of that invariant trivial). $\mathrm{OffBranch}\,x$ says that for every $\ell \neq \mathrm{lineInfty}\,q$ and every point $y$ of either chart over $x$ there is an element $b$ of the corresponding chart algebra whose image is a non-unit of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ and which does not lie in $y$. A further abbreviation $\mathrm{Reads}\,x\,Q$, for $Q$ a place of $\mathrm{xHFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,(q^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$, is introduced — every $f$ with $\mathrm{InStalk}\,x\,f$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and that residue is a non-unit there exactly when $\mathrm{InMax}\,x\,f$ — but it does not occur in the conclusion.
--
--   The conclusion itself: for every $g$ in the subgroup of the group of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphisms of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ generated by the set of those $\tau$ for which there exist $\zeta' \in \mathrm{Idx}\,q$ and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $\tau = \mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$, if the pullback of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ along $g$ differs from $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$, then for all points $x, x'$ of $\mathfrak{X}$ with $\mathrm{GoodPt}\,x$, $\mathrm{OffBranch}\,x$, $\mathrm{GoodPt}\,x'$, $\mathrm{OffBranch}\,x'$, and every place $P$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$: if $\mathrm{Centred}\,P\,x$ then $\mathrm{Centred}\,(g \cdot P)\,x'$ fails.
--
--   This is the separation clause in the construction of the smooth Igusa base model: a level automorphism that does not preserve the Gauss ring of the $\infty$-Igusa branch carries any place centred at a good, off-branch point of the two-chart integral model to a place centred at no such point, so that the residue discs attached to good points of distinct Igusa branches are disjoint away from supersingular $j$-values. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaBaseModel_smoothPointStalks`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaBaseModel_smoothPointStalks).
